From: WF-810DF bring-up

vlanmgr: allow physical port 0

ipq50xx numbers its NSS datapath interfaces from 0 (wan is dp1/if_num 0),
but the vlan manager only accepts physical ports 1..6, so creating wan.<vid>
fails with "wan: 0 is not valid physical port" and the VLAN is never
registered with NSS. QSDK only enables vlan-mgr on ipq807x/ipq60xx, where
port numbering starts at 1, so this assumption was never exercised.

The port arrays use 0 as the empty sentinel, but those walks are confined
to the PPE/VSI paths which are not built for ipq50xx
(NSS_VLAN_MGR_PPE_SUPPORT) and to bonding paths, so accepting 0 is safe on
this target.

--- a/vlan/nss_vlan_mgr.c
+++ b/vlan/nss_vlan_mgr.c
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
 #endif
 #endif /* CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG */
 
-#define NSS_VLAN_PHY_PORT_MIN 1
+#define NSS_VLAN_PHY_PORT_MIN 0
 #define NSS_VLAN_PHY_PORT_MAX 6
 #define NSS_VLAN_PHY_PORT_NUM 8
 #define NSS_VLAN_PHY_PORT_CHK(n) ((n) >= NSS_VLAN_PHY_PORT_MIN && (n) <= NSS_VLAN_PHY_PORT_MAX)
